{
 "cells": [
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Advanced Feature Engineering — Leakage-Safe Forecasting\n","\n","This notebook extends the forecasting dataset with **time-aware temporal, intensity and regional features**. The target remains next-year municipality price growth.\n","\n","> Design principle: every feature must be computable using information available **no later than the municipality's current year**. No future target information is used."]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Feature-engineering strategy\n","\n","The feature set is deliberately richer than Notebook 08, but remains compact because the annual historical sample is relatively short. We add:\n","\n","- second-order temporal lags and momentum;\n","- rolling historical means and volatility;\n","- transaction intensity per 1,000 inhabitants;\n","- log-transformed scale variables;\n","- lagged regional market conditions;\n","- municipality-versus-region relative growth.\n","\n","The resulting dataset can be used by a subsequent notebook for an ablation study: baseline features versus advanced features."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["from pathlib import Path\n","import re\n","import numpy as np\n","import pandas as pd\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","PROJECT_ROOT = Path.cwd()\n","if not (PROJECT_ROOT / 'data').exists(): PROJECT_ROOT = PROJECT_ROOT.parent\n","QUOTATIONS_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / 'data' / 'raw' / 'quotations'\n","TRANSACTIONS_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / 'data' / 'raw' / 'transactions'\n","POPULATION_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / 'data' / 'raw' / 'population'\n","for path in [QUOTATIONS_DIR, TRANSACTIONS_DIR, POPULATION_DIR]:\n","    assert path.exists(), f'Missing source directory: {path}'\n","pd.set_option('display.float_format', lambda x: f'{x:,.4f}')"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Rebuild the annual municipality panel\n","\n","The panel is reconstructed from the raw repository data, following the same source definitions used in the previous forecasting notebooks."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["quotation_parts=[]\n","for path in sorted(QUOTATIONS_DIR.glob('omi_quotations_*.csv')):\n","    match=re.search(r'_(\\d{4})_(S[12])$',path.stem)\n","    if not match: continue\n","    year,semester=int(match.group(1)),match.group(2)\n","    df=pd.read_csv(path,sep=';',low_memory=False)\n","    df.columns=[str(c).replace('\\ufeff','').strip() for c in df.columns]\n","    required=['Comune_ISTAT','Descr_Tipologia','Compr_min','Compr_max','Regione']\n","    missing=[c for c in required if c not in df.columns]\n","    if missing: raise KeyError(f'{path.name}: missing {missing}')\n","    df=df[required].copy()\n","    df['year'],df['semester']=year,semester\n","    quotation_parts.append(df)\n","omi=pd.concat(quotation_parts,ignore_index=True)\n","omi['municipality_code']=omi['Comune_ISTAT'].astype('string').str.strip()\n","omi['Compr_min']=pd.to_numeric(omi['Compr_min'],errors='coerce')\n","omi['Compr_max']=pd.to_numeric(omi['Compr_max'],errors='coerce')\n","omi['price_m2']=omi[['Compr_min','Compr_max']].mean(axis=1)\n","residential=omi[omi['Descr_Tipologia'].astype('string').str.contains('abitazion|villa',case=False,na=False)]\n","semester_panel=(residential.dropna(subset=['municipality_code','price_m2']).groupby(['year','semester','municipality_code'],as_index=False).agg(price_m2=('price_m2','median'),quotation_obs=('price_m2','size'),region=('Regione','first')))\n","annual_price=(semester_panel.groupby(['year','municipality_code'],as_index=False).agg(price_m2=('price_m2','mean'),quotation_obs=('quotation_obs','sum'),region=('region','first'),semesters_available=('semester','nunique')))\n","\n","transaction_parts=[]\n","for folder in sorted(p for p in TRANSACTIONS_DIR.iterdir() if p.is_dir() and p.name.isdigit()):\n","    year=int(folder.name); files=[p for p in folder.iterdir() if p.is_file()]\n","    lista_path=next(p for p in files if 'lista-com' in p.name.lower()); res_path=next(p for p in files if 'valori-res' in p.name.lower())\n","    lista=pd.read_csv(lista_path,sep=';',decimal=','); res=pd.read_csv(res_path,sep=';',decimal=',')\n","    lista.columns=[str(c).strip() for c in lista.columns]; res.columns=[str(c).strip() for c in res.columns]\n","    lista_code=next(c for c in lista.columns if re.search(r'codcom$',c,re.I)); res_code=next(c for c in res.columns if re.search(r'codcom$',c,re.I))\n","    ntn_candidates=[c for c in res.columns if re.fullmatch(r'NTN_?'+str(year),c,re.I)]\n","    if not ntn_candidates: ntn_candidates=[c for c in res.columns if re.match(r'NTN',c,re.I) and 'mq' not in c.lower()]\n","    ntn_col=ntn_candidates[0]\n","    geo_cols=[c for c in [lista_code,'Comune','Provincia','Regione'] if c in lista.columns]\n","    geo=lista[geo_cols].rename(columns={lista_code:'municipality_code'}).copy()\n","    vals=res[[res_code,ntn_col]].rename(columns={res_code:'municipality_code',ntn_col:'ntn'}).copy()\n","    vals['ntn']=pd.to_numeric(vals['ntn'],errors='coerce')\n","    if vals['municipality_code'].duplicated().any(): raise ValueError(f'{year}: duplicate municipality key')\n","    transaction_parts.append(geo.merge(vals,on='municipality_code',how='left',validate='one_to_one').assign(year=year))\n","transactions=pd.concat(transaction_parts,ignore_index=True)\n","\n","population_parts=[]\n","for folder in sorted(p for p in POPULATION_DIR.iterdir() if p.is_dir() and p.name.isdigit()):\n","    year=int(folder.name); path=next(folder.glob('*_Comuni.csv'))\n","    df=pd.read_csv(path,sep=';',encoding='utf-8-sig',usecols=['Codice comune','Età','Totale'])\n","    df.columns=['municipality_code','age','population']\n","    df['municipality_code']=df['municipality_code'].astype('string').str.strip()\n","    df['age']=pd.to_numeric(df['age'],errors='coerce'); df['population']=pd.to_numeric(df['population'],errors='coerce')\n","    population_parts.append(df.loc[df['age'].eq(999),['municipality_code','population']].assign(year=year))\n","population=pd.concat(population_parts,ignore_index=True)\n","\n","market=annual_price.merge(transactions[['year','municipality_code','ntn']],on=['year','municipality_code'],how='left',validate='many_to_one')\n","market=market.merge(population,on=['year','municipality_code'],how='left',validate='many_to_one')\n","market=market.sort_values(['municipality_code','year']).reset_index(drop=True)\n","assert not market.duplicated(['year','municipality_code']).any()\n","print(f'Annual municipality-year rows: {len(market):,}')"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Base growth and scale variables\n","\n","Growth variables are calculated within municipality. Scale variables are transformed with `log1p` where zero values are possible."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["g=market.groupby('municipality_code',group_keys=False)\n","market['price_growth']=g['price_m2'].pct_change()\n","market['ntn_growth']=g['ntn'].pct_change()\n","market['population_growth']=g['population'].pct_change()\n","market['ntn_per_1000']=np.where(market['population'].gt(0),market['ntn']/market['population']*1000,np.nan)\n","market['log_price']=np.log1p(market['price_m2'].clip(lower=0))\n","market['log_ntn']=np.log1p(market['ntn'].clip(lower=0))\n","market['log_population']=np.log1p(market['population'].clip(lower=0))\n","market['target_price_growth']=g['price_growth'].shift(-1)\n","print(market[['price_growth','ntn_growth','population_growth','ntn_per_1000']].describe(percentiles=[.01,.5,.99]).T)"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. Temporal lags, momentum and rolling history\n","\n","For a forecast made at the end of year `t`, all temporal features below use only observations from year `t` or earlier. Rolling statistics are based on the current and preceding historical observations; they never use the future target year."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# Second-order lags\n","n_lags=2\n","for col in ['price_growth','ntn_growth','population_growth','ntn_per_1000','log_price','log_ntn','log_population']:\n","    for lag in range(1,n_lags+1):\n","        market[f'{col}_lag{lag}']=g[col].shift(lag)\n","\n","# Current-year momentum: change in the latest observed growth rate versus the prior year.\n","market['price_momentum_1y']=market['price_growth']-market['price_growth_lag1']\n","market['ntn_momentum_1y']=market['ntn_growth']-market['ntn_growth_lag1']\n","market['population_momentum_1y']=market['population_growth']-market['population_growth_lag1']\n","\n","# Rolling historical statistics. min_periods avoids creating artificial values from a single observation.\n","for col in ['price_growth','ntn_growth','population_growth']:\n","    market[f'{col}_roll2_mean']=g[col].transform(lambda s:s.rolling(2,min_periods=2).mean())\n","    market[f'{col}_roll3_mean']=g[col].transform(lambda s:s.rolling(3,min_periods=2).mean())\n","    market[f'{col}_roll3_std']=g[col].transform(lambda s:s.rolling(3,min_periods=2).std())\n","print(market[['price_growth_lag1','price_growth_lag2','price_growth_roll3_mean','price_growth_roll3_std','price_momentum_1y']].tail())"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 5. Regional context\n","\n","Municipality dynamics can be partly driven by the broader regional market. Regional features are computed from the municipality panel and then lagged, so the forecast for year `t+1` only receives regional information available through year `t`.\n","\n","This is contextual information, not a causal control variable."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["region_year=(market.groupby(['region','year'],as_index=False).agg(region_price_m2=('price_m2','mean'),region_ntn=('ntn','sum'),region_population=('population','sum')))\n","rg=region_year.groupby('region',group_keys=False)\n","region_year['region_price_growth']=rg['region_price_m2'].pct_change()\n","region_year['region_ntn_growth']=rg['region_ntn'].pct_change()\n","region_year['region_population_growth']=rg['region_population'].pct_change()\n","region_year['region_price_growth_lag1']=rg['region_price_growth'].shift(1)\n","region_year['region_ntn_growth_lag1']=rg['region_ntn_growth'].shift(1)\n","region_year['region_population_growth_lag1']=rg['region_population_growth'].shift(1)\n","market=market.merge(region_year[['region','year','region_price_growth_lag1','region_ntn_growth_lag1','region_population_growth_lag1']],on=['region','year'],how='left',validate='many_to_one')\n","market['municipality_minus_region_price_growth_lag1']=market['price_growth_lag1']-market['region_price_growth_lag1']\n","market['municipality_minus_region_ntn_growth_lag1']=market['ntn_growth_lag1']-market['region_ntn_growth_lag1']\n","print(market[['region_price_growth_lag1','region_ntn_growth_lag1','municipality_minus_region_price_growth_lag1']].describe().T)"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 6. Leakage audit\n","\n","The target is next-year price growth. Every feature used for forecasting must be known by the end of the current year. The audit below documents the intended information timing explicitly."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["feature_timing=pd.DataFrame([\n","    ('price_growth','t','current'),('ntn_growth','t','current'),('population_growth','t','current'),\n","    ('price_growth_lag1','t-1','historical'),('price_growth_lag2','t-2','historical'),\n","    ('ntn_growth_lag1','t-1','historical'),('ntn_growth_lag2','t-2','historical'),\n","    ('population_growth_lag1','t-1','historical'),('population_growth_lag2','t-2','historical'),\n","    ('ntn_per_1000','t','current'),('ntn_per_1000_lag1','t-1','historical'),\n","    ('log_price_lag1','t-1','historical'),('log_ntn_lag1','t-1','historical'),('log_population_lag1','t-1','historical'),\n","    ('price_growth_roll2_mean','through t','historical'),('price_growth_roll3_mean','through t','historical'),('price_growth_roll3_std','through t','historical'),\n","    ('ntn_growth_roll2_mean','through t','historical'),('ntn_growth_roll3_mean','through t','historical'),('ntn_growth_roll3_std','through t','historical'),\n","    ('population_growth_roll2_mean','through t','historical'),('population_growth_roll3_mean','through t','historical'),('population_growth_roll3_std','through t','historical'),\n","    ('region_price_growth_lag1','t-1','regional historical'),('region_ntn_growth_lag1','t-1','regional historical'),\n","    ('region_population_growth_lag1','t-1','regional historical'),('municipality_minus_region_price_growth_lag1','t-1','derived historical'),\n","    ('municipality_minus_region_ntn_growth_lag1','t-1','derived historical')\n","] ,"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["### Audit rule\n","\n","`target_price_growth` is explicitly shifted one year forward. Features such as current-year growth and rolling statistics through year `t` are therefore legitimate predictors of year `t+1`. No feature is allowed to reference `t+1` or later."]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 7. Feature quality and modeling dataset\n","\n","We retain a compact set of advanced predictors and report missingness before modeling. Missing values are expected for early years where lags and rolling windows cannot yet be formed; downstream models can impute them inside a pipeline."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["advanced_features=[\n","    'price_growth','ntn_growth','population_growth','ntn_per_1000',\n","    'price_growth_lag1','price_growth_lag2','ntn_growth_lag1','ntn_growth_lag2','population_growth_lag1','population_growth_lag2',\n","    'price_momentum_1y','ntn_momentum_1y','population_momentum_1y',\n","    'price_growth_roll2_mean','price_growth_roll3_mean','price_growth_roll3_std',\n","    'ntn_growth_roll2_mean','ntn_growth_roll3_mean','ntn_growth_roll3_std',\n","    'population_growth_roll2_mean','population_growth_roll3_mean','population_growth_roll3_std',\n","    'ntn_per_1000_lag1','ntn_per_1000_lag2','log_price_lag1','log_ntn_lag1','log_population_lag1',\n","    'region_price_growth_lag1','region_ntn_growth_lag1','region_population_growth_lag1',\n","    'municipality_minus_region_price_growth_lag1','municipality_minus_region_ntn_growth_lag1'\n","]\n","model_data=market[['municipality_code','year','region','price_m2','ntn','population','target_price_growth']+advanced_features].copy()\n","model_data=model_data.dropna(subset=['target_price_growth']).reset_index(drop=True)\n","missing=(model_data[advanced_features].isna().mean().sort_values(ascending=False).rename('missing_rate').to_frame())\n","display(missing)\n","print(f'Final modeling rows: {len(model_data):,}')\n","print(f'Features: {len(advanced_features)}')"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 8. Export the feature dataset\n","\n","The processed dataset is written to `data/processed/forecasting_features.csv` for reuse by the next modeling notebook. The raw sources remain the reproducible source of truth."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"source":["OUTPUT_DIR=PROJECT_ROOT/'data'/'processed'\n","OUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\n","output_path=OUTPUT_DIR/'forecasting_features.csv'\n","model_data.to_csv(output_path,index=False)\n","print(f'Saved: {output_path}')"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 9. What comes next\n","\n","Notebook 10 should perform a controlled **feature ablation and final benchmark**: compare the Notebook 08 baseline feature set against these advanced features using the same rolling-origin folds. The key question is not whether the feature set improves in-sample fit, but whether it improves out-of-sample MAE/RMSE consistently across forecast years.\n","\n","Potential extensions after that benchmark include time-aware hyperparameter tuning, macroeconomic variables and explicit spatial features."]}
